.TH DICONVHIST 8
.SH NAME
diconvhist \- add Message-IDs from an INN history file to Diablo's dhistory
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B diconvhist
[
.B \-f
]
[
.B \-C
.I diablo.config
]
[
.B \-V
]
.I innhistory
|
.B \-
.SH DESCRIPTION
.I diconvhist
reads an INN history file (or standard input for '-') and adds each
Message-ID it doesn't already know to Diablo's dhistory as an expired
entry.  diablo then refuses those articles when peers offer them again,
which avoids refetching what the old INN server already had during a
switch from INN to Diablo.  It can run while diablo is running.
.PP
It prints the lines scanned, the entries added, the duplicates and the
ignored lines every 1000 lines and at the end.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.B \-f
Fast mode: after 10 Message-IDs in a row that are already in dhistory,
skip the next 100 lines without looking them up.
.TP
.BI \-C " diablo.config"
Use this diablo.config instead of the default.
.TP
.B \-V
Print the version and exit.
.SH BUGS
Only lines that begin with a Message-ID in angle brackets are used.  INN
2.x writes the history in hashed form ("[hash]"), so its history file
gives no entries; it works with the older text format only.
.SH "SEE ALSO"
diablo(8),
diload(8),
didump(8),
diablo-files(5)
